+{"entries":{"dd76d45f5c77269fd1145c8a5d754f253d513503c2face7a3cf94b705d1c108d":{"cache_key":"dd76d45f5c77269fd1145c8a5d754f253d513503c2face7a3cf94b705d1c108d","key_text":"manager:Plan and decompose goal into tasks\n## Goal\nImplement @.scratch/apex-lsp-gaps/issues/01-semantic-tokens-implement.md","response":"Decomposed goal into 2 tasks: d416253d0c47 (architect: write the missing implementation spec at .scratch/apex-lsp-gaps/issues/01-semantic-tokens-implement.md) and 01ebe22cbb5f (backend: implement semantic-tokens capability + handlers + integration tests, depends_on d416253d0c47). Research already covered the design (.scratch/apex-lsp-gaps/research.md synthesis item 1); no new binder work needed. Tests are baked into task 2 rather than split into a separate QA task -- avoids fragmenting a single feature.","word_vector":{"manager":0.05263157894736842,"plan":0.05263157894736842,"and":0.05263157894736842,"decompose":0.05263157894736842,"goal":0.10526315789473684,"into":0.05263157894736842,"tasks":0.05263157894736842,"implement":0.10526315789473684,"scratch":0.05263157894736842,"apex":0.05263157894736842,"lsp":0.05263157894736842,"gaps":0.05263157894736842,"issues":0.05263157894736842,"01":0.05263157894736842,"semantic":0.05263157894736842,"tokens":0.05263157894736842,"md":0.05263157894736842},"model":"agent","hit_count":10,"created_at":1788584760.3658884,"last_used_at":1788585034.817381,"verified":false,"git_diff_lines":0,"source_task_id":"c93b7dc523e2"},"00a338c32489538d454fe9a04deef4714c56cf16f289c75bfcc173d08018f49d":{"cache_key":"00a338c32489538d454fe9a04deef4714c56cf16f289c75bfcc173d08018f49d","key_text":"architect:Write semantic-tokens implementation spec\n## Goal\nProduce the implementation spec that ticket `.scratch/apex-lsp-gaps/issues/01-semantic-tokens-implement.md` should contain. This file does not yet exist; the goal `Implement @.scratch/apex-lsp-gaps/issues/01-semantic-tokens-implement.md` cannot start without it. All background research is already done -- read `.scratch/apex-lsp-gaps/research.md` first (semantic tokens is item #1 in the synthesis section, lines 73-76). Your job is to turn that research into an executable spec the backend can implement mechanically.\n\n## Deliverable\nA single markdown file at `.scratch/apex-lsp-gaps/issues/01-semantic-tokens-implement.md`, style-matching the existing `.scratch/apex-diagnostics/issues/*-implement.md` tickets. No code changes.\n\n## Required contents\n1. **`SemanticTokensLegend`** -- the exact list of `SemanticTokenType`s and `SemanticTokenModifier`s the server will declare in `initialize`. Pick from the LSP 3.17 standard sets (see `lsp-types = 0.95.0` -- the crate is already in `crates/apexls-server/Cargo.toml`). Only include types the mapping below actually emits; omit `event`, `regexp`, `macro`, etc. that Apex has no analogue for.\n2. **`SymbolKind` -> token-type mapping** at *declaration* sites. Every `apex_binder::symbol::SymbolKind` variant (`crates/apex-binder/src/symbol.rs:40-55`: Class, Interface, Enum, EnumConstant, Trigger, Method, Constructor, Field, Property, Parameter, LocalVar, CatchVar, ForEachVar, SwitchBindingVar) must have a specified target token type or an explicit \"skip\" note.\n3. **`Resolution` -> token-type mapping** at *reference* sites. Every `apex_binder::reference_table::Resolution` variant (`crates/apex-binder/src/reference_table.rs:127-136`: Resolved(SymbolId), Candidates, SchemaObject, UnknownSchema, StdlibMember, Label, VisualforcePage, Unresolved) needs a rule -- e.g. `Resolved` looks up the target symbol's `SymbolKind` and reuses the declaration mapping; `StdlibMember` with `member: None` becomes `class`, with `member: Some(_)` becomes `method` (or `property` -- decide based on whether we can tell them apart from `StdlibMemberRef` alone; if not, pick one and note the ceiling). Cover the edge cases explicitly.\n4. **Modifier mapping** -- how `apex_binder::symbol::ModifierSet` (same file, lines 95-120) fields become `SemanticTokenModifier` bits. At minimum: `is_static` -> `STATIC`, `is_final` -> `READONLY`, `Visibility::Global`/`Public`/`Protected`/`Private` (specify), declaration site -> `DECLARATION`, and note that `defaultLibrary` should be set for `StdlibMember`/`SchemaObject`/`UnknownSchema` reference kinds.\n5. **Range vs full**: declare both `full: true` and `range: true` in the capability options; explicitly do NOT implement delta (`edits`) in v1 -- note it as a follow-up.\n6. **Encoding**: standard LSP delta encoding (line-delta, start-char-delta, length, type-index, modifier-bitset), UTF-8/16/32 aware via the existing `line_index::PositionEncoding` (`crates/apexls-server/src/line_index.rs`).\n7. **Handler shape**: `Backend::semantic_tokens_full` and `Backend::semantic_tokens_range` follow the existing snapshot + `wait_for_rebuild` + `bind.program` pattern used by every other handler in `crates/apexls-server/src/lib.rs` (see `Backend::document_symbol` line 1250 as the closest reference).\n8. **Where the walk goes**: `pub(crate) fn semantic_tokens_full(program: &BoundProgram, file: FileId) -> SemanticTokens` and `_range(..., range: TextRange)` in `crates/apexls-server/src/capabilities.rs`, alongside the existing per-feature functions.\n9. **Tests**: a new `crates/apexls-server/tests/semantic_tokens.rs` integration test file, at least one test per major token category (class decl, method decl, field decl, local, parameter, static call, stdlib call, unresolved) driven by a small inline Apex source string. Follow the existing `crates/apexls-server/tests/document_symbol*.rs` / `folding_range*.rs` style (which does exist -- confirm by listing that dir).\n10. **Acceptance criteria** and **non-goals** (explicitly: no delta, no dynamic registration, no re-highlighting on hover, no per-token debug tooltips).\n\n## Context hints\n- Existing per-capability functions live in `crates/apexls-server/src/capabilities.rs` (grep `pub(crate) fn` for the naming convention -- new fns should be named `semantic_tokens_full`/`semantic_tokens_range`).\n- The `initialize` capability block is `crates/apexls-server/src/lib.rs:657-758` -- new field slots in alphabetically-ish alongside `selection_range_provider`.\n- `apex-syntax`'s CST walk primitives are what the token producer will iterate over; the binder's `ReferenceTable`/`SymbolTable` supply per-node kinds -- no new binder work is needed per the research doc (\"Cost: moderate ... no new binder work needed.\").\n- No new crate deps -- `lsp-types 0.95` already re-exports `SemanticTokens`, `SemanticTokensLegend`, `SemanticTokenType`, `SemanticTokenModifier`, `SemanticTokensServerCapabilities`.\n\n## When done\n1. `git add .scratch/apex-lsp-gaps/issues/01-semantic-tokens-implement.md && git commit -m \"spec: semantic-tokens ticket 01\"`\n2. `bernstein task complete <this-task-id> --summary \"Wrote implementation spec for semantic tokens.\"`","response":"Wrote implementation spec for semantic tokens.","word_vector":{"architect":0.0013966480446927375,"write":0.0013966480446927375,"semantic":0.0111731843575419,"tokens":0.0111731843575419,"implementation":0.004189944134078212,"spec":0.006983240223463687,"goal":0.002793296089385475,"produce":0.0013966480446927375,"the":0.036312849162011177,"that":0.006983240223463687,"ticket":0.002793296089385475,"scratch":0.008379888268156424,"apex":0.015363128491620111,"lsp":0.012569832402234637,"gaps":0.006983240223463687,"issues":0.006983240223463687,"01":0.006983240223463687,"implement":0.0111731843575419,"md":0.008379888268156424,"should":0.004189944134078212,"contain":0.0013966480446927375,"this":0.002793296089385475,"file":0.006983240223463687,"does":0.002793296089385475,"not":0.004189944134078212,"yet":0.0013966480446927375,"exist":0.002793296089385475,"cannot":0.0013966480446927375,"start":0.002793296089385475,"without":0.0013966480446927375,"it":0.002793296089385475,"all":0.0013966480446927375,"background":0.0013966480446927375,"research":0.00558659217877095,"is":0.00837988826815