capabilities are declared statically in `initialize` like every other feature in this crate.\n\n## Validation before marking complete\nAll of these must pass locally, from repo root:\n- `cargo build -p apexls-server` (the primary compile gate)\n- `cargo test -p apexls-server --test semantic_tokens -- --nocapture` (this task's new integration tests)\n- `cargo test -p apexls-server` (regression: no other test file breaks -- if one does, that's a real bug in the wiring, don't disable it)\n- `cargo clippy -p apexls-server -- -D warnings` if the repo uses it (check first with `git grep clippy .cargo/`)\n\n## Context hints\n- Snapshot + wait_for_rebuild pattern: `Backend::document_symbol` at `crates/apexls-server/src/lib.rs:1250-1273` is the closest existing shape to copy from.\n- Per-capability function convention: every `pub(crate) fn` in `crates/apexls-server/src/capabilities.rs` takes `&BoundProgram` and `FileId`, and returns the plain `lsp-types` return shape (not a `Result`) -- errors bubble via `Option::None` or empty vecs. Keep this convention.\n- `line_index::PositionEncoding` in `crates/apexls-server/src/line_index.rs` already handles UTF-8/16/32 line/column conversion; use its existing methods, don't reinvent.\n- Binder data sources: `BoundProgram::symbol(SymbolId) -> &Symbol` gives you kind + modifiers; `program.reference_table_for(file).get(SyntaxPtr)` gives you `Resolution` -- both already used all over `capabilities.rs` (grep for `references_to` and `resolution_at`).\n- Test-file style: existing tests build a `Backend` in-process via `binder_integration.rs` helpers -- reuse that infrastructure rather than spawning a real subprocess.\n\n## When done\n1. `git add -A && git commit -m \"feat: LSP semantic tokens (ticket 01)\"`\n2. `bernstein task complete <this-task-id> --summary \"Implemented semantic tokens with tests.\"`", "role": "backend", "priority": 2, "scope": "large", "complexity": "medium", "estimated_minutes": 240, "status": "open", "task_type": "sta